 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Something happens although",
     "texto": [
      "To say that something happens despite something else, use **-(으)ㄴ데도 / -는데도 / -인데도** (even though, despite): 피곤하다 → **피곤한데도** (even though I'm tired), 비가 오다 → **비가 왔는데도** (even though it rained), 공부하다 → **공부하는데도** (even though I study), 학생이다 → **학생인데도** (even though I am a student).",
      "비가 **왔는데도** 나갔어요 = even though it rained, I went out."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Difference with -지만",
     "texto": [
      "**-지만** joins two ideas with a normal contrast. **-(으)ㄴ데도** puts more emphasis on how surprising the situation is.",
      "피곤하지만 일했어요 = I was tired, but I worked. 피곤한데도 일했어요 = even though I was tired, I worked (more surprising)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
